---
import Layout from "@components/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "@components/PageHeader.astro";
import { List, Card } from "webcoreui/astro";
---

<Layout title="Resources & Conclusion - Replenish Guide">
    <PageHeader
        title="Conclusion & Resources"
        description="Comprehensive acknowledgments honoring the theorists, pioneers, and tournament pilots of the Premodern Replenish Discord community, alongside curated reading lists and project roadmaps."
        imageSrc="/src/assets/banners/theory.jpeg"
        imageAlt="Premodern Replenish Strategic Theory Banner"
        imageCaption="Premodern competitive theory is a collaborative, evolving endeavor driven by passionate tournament pilots and community researchers."
        isCard={true}
    />

    <Card title="Acknowledgments & Community Credits" titleTag="h2">
        <p style="margin-top: 0;">
            This exhaustive compendium is the culmination of years of
            theoretical refinement, tournament playtesting, and passionate
            community collaboration within the Premodern ecosystem. Special
            gratitude belongs to <strong>Brian Siu (Dr Siuss)</strong> for penning
            the definitive foundational primer that inspired this modern interactive
            guide, and to <strong>Gary Roth</strong> for his rigorous mathematical
            treatises documenting the formal physics and stack interactions of Opalescent
            Parallax Wave collisions.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
            Most importantly, profound credit is owed to the enthusiastic
            pilots, deckbuilders, and theorists of the <strong
                >Premodern Replenish Discord community</strong
            >. In particular, notable tournament innovations and strategic
            frameworks from
            <strong>Marinebiomancer</strong> (pioneer of the "Creatureless 75" hard-control
            lock),
            <strong>AchiIIes</strong> (architect of pre-ban Parallax Tide dominance),
            <strong>Bryan Gulotta</strong> (proactive game-1 disruption theorist),
            and
            <strong>Alessandro Galli</strong> directly shaped the maindeck analyses
            and sideboard methodologies featured across these pages. Substantial analytical
            insights, mulligan heuristics, and granular matchup evaluations were cultivated
            directly from their rigorous daily discussions and match reporting within
            the channel.
        </p>
    </Card>

    <Card title="Project Backlog & Roadmap" titleTag="h2">
        <p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
            This guide is an actively curated, living document designed to
            evolve alongside the competitive Premodern metagame. Below is our
            transparent engineering backlog of feature upgrades and expansions
            currently under active development:
        </p>
        <ul style="padding-left: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                <strong>Mobile UI & Responsiveness Optimization:</strong> Fine-tuning
                spacing across our interactive sideboard matrices, card analysis tables,
                and mobile navigation layouts to guarantee a flawless reading experience
                on compact touchscreens.
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                <strong>Ongoing Metagame & Matchup Maintenance:</strong> Regularly
                refreshing sideboard transformation configurations, threat matrices,
                and flex slot recommendations as post-ban regional championship trends
                solidify.
            </li>
            <li style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                <strong>Championship Decklist Archive:</strong> Expanding the tournament
                showcase with emerging Top 8 tournament decklists and analytical post-mortem
                evaluations from upcoming premier live events.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </Card>

    <Card title="External Resources & Further Reading" titleTag="h2">
        <List
            itemGroups={[
                {
                    items: [
                        {
                            name: "Original Replenish Primer",
                            subText: "by Brian Siu (Dr Siuss)",
                            href: "https://squeeshouseofpizza.com/en-brl/pages/replenish-primer-brian-siu",
                            target: "_blank",
                        },
                        {
                            name: "External Interference in Opalescent Parallax Waves",
                            subText: "by Gary Roth (December 2024)",
                            href: "https://docs.google.com/document/d/e/2PACX-1vTS7yvU3FLB3Y2tPfV5EX8IEKFtGmMYDLAmKHieoIV90dbmX7jcu-C_dImJpM3ZU0w5zLt3hF_QuwCM/pub",
                            target: "_blank",
                        },
                        {
                            name: "On the Physics of Collisions Between Opalescent Parallax Waves",
                            subText: "by Gary Roth (September 2024)",
                            href: "https://docs.google.com/document/d/e/2PACX-1vQEW3hgl_gxjLwuTjdH5hoIZKxWNXAUotSipazs2pv60AzC0CUuwrjxjINJkgVfnKOquMgIgm6HZHc4/pub",
                            target: "_blank",
                        },
                        {
                            name: "Ban List Update 2026",
                            subText:
                                "by Martin Berlin (January 2026) on premodernmagic.com",
                            href: "https://premodernmagic.com/blog/ban-list-update-2026/",
                            target: "_blank",
                        },
                        {
                            name: "Monster of the Week Episode 101: Replenish 2.0",
                            subText: "(February 2026) on Wak-Wak",
                            href: "https://www.wak-wak.se/monster/2026-2-5/episode-101-replenish-20",
                            target: "_blank",
                        },
                    ],
                },
            ]}
        />
    </Card>
</Layout>
